  "letter": {
    "premise": "To every soul who showed up, stayed up late, gave up comfortable choices, and poured themselves into something that had never been made before —",
    "point": "thank you."
  },
  "quote": {
    "text": "A hero is an ordinary individual who finds the strength to persevere and endure in spite of overwhelming obstacles.",
    "emphasis": "persevere and endure",
    "attribution": "Christopher Reeve"
  },
  "reflection": {
    "eyebrow": "What happened in 2026",
    "countLabel": "people, artists, collectives and organisations made ODDfest 2026. Together.",
    "body": "Creative Week ran June 8–14. Partner events across Helsinki brought in more than 1,000 people. ODDference took two days — more than 50 speakers, more than 30 sessions. ODDfest opened on the Friday and ran through Saturday — more than 150 acts across central Helsinki, from Vanha Ylioppilastalo to Tavastia, with its own programme of talks on top.\n\nNone of it was ODD's alone. Curators from dance, film, music, games and research shaped the programme. Artists brought their own work, their own crews and their own crowds. Volunteers kept things calm when they got chaotic, and they did get chaotic. Partners, venues and foundations joined the oddness before anyone knew how it would turn out.\n\nThe theme was Bravery. Turned out it wasn't just a theme.",
    "closing": "Every one of them is named below. That's the point."
  },
